# The Planetary Council's window on the election of a governor (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c; opened with council_gov, which is
# council(1, 0, 1), after votes_all has given every faction one vote, so that all may stand). The panel lists the candidates and
# their votes at its foot, but the original's drawing of it gives up when the list is longer than three (it draws the panel again
# with no list in it): five may stand here, and the list is empty. The button that chooses (id 4, the one with the whole width)
# opens a popup of the candidates and Abstain; one is picked and OK made; every faction has then voted, and the window decides
# (make_resolution picks the winner by the votes, the turn deciding a tie) and shows who was elected, with the seats rearranged
# round the governor (the leaders are drawn again, the middle seat the governor's). Escape closes the window and the game carries
# out the election. Then a second election, with the new governor in the middle seat and distinct votes (two candidates stand, the
# list is shown, the player Abstains), and a third with no governor and a tie for second (three stand, the third line of the list
# in the middle of the panel), where a click on a seat asks the leader for his vote for a candidate (the popup of the candidates; the first
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
